    <statement><p>What is the length of an arc cut off by an angle of 2.5 radians on a
circle of radius 4 inches?</p>
<p><fillin characters="18" name="AnSwEr0001"/> (include units: )</p>
</statement>
    <answer>
      <p>
        <m>10\ {\rm in}</m>
      </p>
    </answer>
    <solution><alert>  SOLUTION </alert>




The arc length, <m>s</m>, corresponding to an angle of <m>\theta</m> radians in a circle of radius <m>r</m> is <m>s = r \cdot \theta</m>.



Thus our arc length is <m>s = ( 4 ) ( 2.5 ) = 10 \mbox{in}</m>





</solution>
